  "description": "Maker operations: what the bot is quoting, what it decided, and whether its inputs are alive. Rows top to bottom answer, in order: is it quoting near fair value and is it alive; what did each tick decide and under which regime; how is inventory tracking; and are the feeds healthy. One market at a time via the selector, except the heartbeat, feed-health, and tick-error panels, which are process-wide by design. Every table here is written by the maker bot fire-and-forget: a gap can mean the bot stopped OR that its writes are failing, and only the container logs separate those two.",
  "editable": true,
  "graphTooltip": 1,
  "links": [],
  "panels": [
    {
      "datasource": {
        "type": "postgres",
        "uid": "dropset-postgres"
      },
      "description": "The composed fair value against the book actually resting on-chain, with takes overlaid. Read the gap, not the levels: `fair value` vs `reference (on-chain)` is the drift the trigger policy is tolerating, and `reference (candidate)` is where this tick would move it. A `best bid`/`best ask` that stops while fair value continues means that side went dark (a freeze-side, a halt, or a book killed for staleness) \u2014 the series ends rather than dropping to zero, which is why nulls are never spanned here. Fills are scaled out of the indexer's raw atoms ratio; see the panel query.",
