      "description": "Every registered feed source's current liveness, written by the framework's metrics seam rather than by any per-feed wiring \u2014 so a venue adapter added later appears here on its first poll with no change to this dashboard. Not filtered by market: a source is shared across the roster. `ok_age_secs` is measured off `last_ok_at` alone, which is the point of tracking it separately from `last_error_at` \u2014 a feed erroring on every retry would look fresh by a single `updated_at`. A row with status `ok` and a populated `last_error` has RECOVERED; the error text is kept deliberately so a flap remains diagnosable after the fact.",
